WEBVTT

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:16.500
If we win this contest, Akari,
you've gotta join Cyedge!

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.830
Wha--?!

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.000
Job poacher!

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.830
What's the matter? Afraid to lose?

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:23.200
Grr!

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.290
--C-Calm down, Akari.
--And how about if I win?!

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.910
I'll grovel, dance naked, or whatever you want!

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:34.830
I don't wanna see it, but you're on!
Don't forget your promise!

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:37.660
Fine! It's settled then.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.120
A-Are you sure about making a promise like that?

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.790
What?! We've just gotta win!

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:46.830
B-But...

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:52.580
Doesn't it make you mad?!
He's totally making fun of our company!

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.080
Akari...

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:59.450
Well, it makes me mad!
It's just like insulting my family!

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:03.500
You're right. Yeah... Let's win!

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.700
<i>Let's dive right into today's letters</i>

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:17.250
<i>It's "Personal Advice" and the title is</i>

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.250
<i>"Hurry into Love! Hurry Love! Love!!"</i>

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.830
<i>Hey, hear me out.</i>
<i>There's something I really wanna say</i>

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:39.040
<i>You've got courage to follow</i>
<i>your dreams which is why I chose you</i>

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.160
<i>Is it a risky bet</i>

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:46.620
<i>Despite no experience,</i>
<i>we jumped right in together</i>

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.080
<i>And this unpredictable story</i>

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.200
<i>Is your creation--</i>
<i>a heart-throbbing innovation</i>

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.660
<i>Quickly! Quickly! Take me along</i>

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.290
<i>On a bittersweet love venture</i>

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:06.080
<i>Ah! Measured not by skill</i>
<i>but by scale and romance</i>

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:11.120
<i>Hurry! Hurry! Boldly, subtly, show your appeal</i>

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.160
<i>Ah! Our meeting was a miracle</i>
<i>that can't be neglected</i>

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.750
<i>It's galactic level</i>

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:23.250
<i>I see. Sounds like you're head over heels.</i>

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:28.540
<i>Let's tell him, just like battle</i>

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.910
<i>"Hurry into Love! Hurry Love! Love!!"</i>

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:33.290
<i>Everyone, Hurry! Hurry Love! Love!!</i>

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.290
"Episode Three: Order Contest"
More questions?

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.580
We've fallen way behind.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:43.450
'Cause our president walks slower
than a newborn fawn.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.870
S-Sorry.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:51.160
Um, let's see... Which person
might scrutinize financial decisions?

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:56.910
One: Top banana. Two: Bean counter.
Three: Hot potato.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:00.580
Hmm. Can't say I know much about plants.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:04.040
I've got this, President!
I'm good at this stuff!

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:10.250
Oh, right! Makoto's hobbies are collecting
plants and studying maju!

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:15.120
President! Trust your employees
when it's their field of expertise!

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.870
R-Right. Go for it, Makoto.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.830
The answer to this is two: "bean counter."

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:27.660
But it's not referring to actual beans.
It's just a nickname for accountants.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:32.660
Whoa, nice!

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:35.450
That's my little brother!

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:38.120
For plants and maju, I'm your guy!

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.910
Now then, let's hurry onward!

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:44.250
We don't want those Cyedge guys beating us!

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:55.910
Hey. How did you become interested
in researching maju and plants?

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:59.080
Hmm... I wonder what it was.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.790
Makoto was kinda frail back when he was young...

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:05.580
...so he spent lots of time reading books.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.290
Oh, yeah.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:12.410
I always lost track of time since
it's so much fun learning new things.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:14.830
I bet I picked it up then.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:18.950
You once gave Akari a sialme flower
as a present?

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.120
Oh. Did she tell you that?

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.700
Jeez, can't you keep your mouth shut?

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:27.290
Sorry. I didn't think it was some big secret.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:32.250
Yeah. I saw sialme in a book
and thought it was perfect for her.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.950
What a wonderful brother and sister you two are!

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:38.200
Y-You think?

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:43.540
Makoto actually discovered
a new species of legged slaby!

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.830
Legged slaby?

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:51.620
You know, this dungeon's so full of
rare plants that it makes me giddy!

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.250
For example...

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:57.500
This ground sesame shakes
its leaves if you go near it!

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.250
Wow, you're right!

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:04.290
This red-eyed Susan is perfect
for waking up after an all-nighter!

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.000
Yeah? You know your stuff!

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.700
Maybe you should take up collecting plants too!

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.910
You can even use 'em to make medicine and stuff!

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:18.040
T-True. That kind of medicine
sounds scary though.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:22.120
Knock it off, you two!
We're not here to round up leaves.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:25.620
We came to beat Diver and get first place!

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:29.040
I get that, Sis. It's Rivar, though...

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:32.830
Oh! I found an interesting plant!

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.000
Kinda looks like a necktie.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.120
Ack! President! Not that!

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.160
Huh? Wh-What is it?!

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.000
Th-That's a restructroot!

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.040
Restructroot?

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:52.330
Yeah. When it's pulled out,
anyone who hears its final scream of agony...

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:55.540
A-Am I gonna die?!

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:59.500
...will be cursed by restructuring
within the week!

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.660
Talk about highly specific!

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.120
Such a merciless cost-cutter!

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:06.540
You mean he's gonna get sacked?!

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:10.160
That's awful! We finally found a home for him!

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:14.750
Y-You make it sound like
I'm a stray cat or dog. Oh, man...

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:19.790
I'll do something about this!
Stay back and don't look!

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:22.200
And plug your ears to be safe!

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.330
B-But...

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:25.330
I'll be fine! Hurry!

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.620
President! Let's do as he says!

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.580
He's a plant pro after all!

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:33.120
Have faith in my brother!

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:36.040
A-All right... It's all you!

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:42.540
Huh? Wh-What's that sound?

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:46.370
Let's not worry about that, President.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:50.120
There's things in this world better not to know.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:53.500
Just relax and let Makoto take care of it.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.410
I-I know, but...

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:59.620
Mmm! Now that's what I call tasty!

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:05.250
I-Is there actually something in there?

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:07.910
I swear I saw eyes or something...

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:10.200
President! We're good now!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.910
O-Okay!

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:16.580
Man, what a surprise!
Never thought we'd see restructroot here!

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:20.080
To be honest, it doesn't belong
in a place like this.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.410
It might've been a trap set by the Agency!

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:26.160
Well, at least our president's safe.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:29.700
It would stink if we lost him to restructuring.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:35.910
U-Um, Makoto? About just now...

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:38.200
Huh? What's wrong, President?

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.750
N-Nothing!

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.750
Damn this plant!

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:45.410
Huh? That voice...

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:49.830
I think a certain someone
made the same mistake as you.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:50.910
Let's go help!

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:55.200
Huh? Are you kidding me?
This is a huge chance for us!

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.500
We could pull ahead of Cyedge if we leave him.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.410
I know we'd be helping our enemy.

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:07.330
But still, data says that building
a convenience store

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:11.330
next to another increases profits for both.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:16.040
Argh, sheesh! I don't agree with it, but fine!

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:19.330
Let's help and get this over with.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:20.370
Eww!

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:29.160
That was uncalled for. And what the hell
was that freakish plant anyways?

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:33.950
D-Don't look at me like that!
I don't remember asking for help!

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:40.830
Now, now, Rivar. Go on and thank
them like a proper working adult.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.870
Shut up! It's gonna be us in Cyedge that wins!

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:45.950
I'll never hand over the order form kirakuri!

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:48.160
Wha--?! How ungrateful!

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.950
I told you Wiper's the worst!

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:54.120
For the last time, his name's Rivar.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:57.620
Let's hurry up!
At this rate, he'll reach the kirakuri--

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:01.950
Y-You don't think...?

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:08.580
That's...!

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.950
It's the boss of this place!

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:16.910
A three-headed maju with a boss,
management, and subordinate head.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.950
Now there's a boss who's a pain in the neck!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.040
Damn this thing!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:29.040
Rivar! Don't let all the heads throw you off!

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:33.290
I know that, but it's hard
to keep track of 'em all!

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:38.160
They're struggling!

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:43.450
With three heads, it's probably
as tough as three maju combined.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:45.790
It might be too much for them.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:52.700
Guys, let's help 'em out!
We can't just sit and watch!

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.950
Even after his betrayal?

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:59.790
He's a fellow adventurer!
We've gotta help each other out!

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:02.040
So be it then!

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:06.410
Since Viper's in way over his head,
let's lend a hand!

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.870
Sis, it's Rivar...

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.450
Let's go, guys! Time to attack!

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:17.370
Since you're hopeless, we're here to help!

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:19.330
I-I don't need your help!

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:24.830
I couldn't care less! Unless we take
'em out, we're stuck here too!

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:28.200
Tsk! You better stay out of our way.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:31.250
You're all bark and no bite! Let's go!

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:36.080
Don't focus too much on one head!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:43.120
They're faring better with Akari helping, but...

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.370
It's tougher than I thought!

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:51.000
What are you doing?!
I told you to stay out of my...!

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.620
I-It's just...

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:00.750
...too strong!

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:05.120
I-It's no use...

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:07.580
At this rate, we'll get wiped out.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:15.750
Shit! How the hell do we take it down?!

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:18.040
President! What's our strategy?!

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.830
Hmm. Speaking of those heads...

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:34.370
If it's a subordinate, management, and boss...

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:36.910
I've got it!

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:40.870
You guys! Don't attack from the same side!

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:44.000
Split two ways and use their blind spot!

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:44.950
Huh?

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:46.410
Say what?

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:49.080
Akari, get the subordinate on bottom!

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.830
Rivar, hit the boss on top!

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:54.620
Don't let them see it coming!

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:57.000
Everyone else, try to distract it!

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.370
Affirmative!

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:00.080
Got it, President!

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:02.370
I'm not so sure, but all right!

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:06.040
Hey, check this out! Over here!

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:10.290
Take... this!

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:20.750
The bottom head is mine! You get the one on top!

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:23.450
Hmph! I don't take orders from him.

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:27.870
Now's not the time to complain.
Would you rather get wiped out?

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:30.750
Tsk! I'm only doing this once! Just once!

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:36.540
Yeah!

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.330
Huh? Are they...?

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:52.660
The heads started fighting?

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:55.250
The boss and subordinate are going at it...

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:59.500
...and poor management is caught in the middle!

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:02.370
Oh! Was this your plan all along?

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:08.290
Yup! I wanted to make the boss
and subordinate think they hit each other.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:16.870
Whoa. They're so busy fighting,
they don't care about us.

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:20.830
Yeah. I never imagined
it would work out this well.

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:26.120
Wha--? This happening was something he planned?

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:29.290
As I thought. He must be...

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:33.290
Now's our chance!
The subordinate's scared of getting fired!

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:37.120
I guess even maju fear restructuring!

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:38.910
L-Let's do this!

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:57.370
Whew! I guess it all worked out!

00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:00.080
Hmph. Couldn't have done it without us.

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:04.750
You're still saying crap like that?!
It's all thanks to our president!

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:08.500
Well, Rivar did cooperate and fight with us...

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:12.750
Sh-Shut up. More importantly,
this contest ain't over yet!

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:14.950
Wha--?! Now that you mention it...!

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:17.910
You snooze, you lose!

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:20.160
--Hey!
--I got dibs on the order form kirakuri!

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.120
--I got dibs on the order form kirakuri!

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.450
Victory will finally be our--!

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:31.450
It's... gone!
The order form kirakuri is... gone!

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.750
What? You're right!

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:35.870
Don't tell me you...!

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:39.330
N-No! I swear I didn't touch it!

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.580
Then, who could have...?

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:45.290
I'm the one who took the kirakuri.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:46.290
Huh?

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:51.370
Wh-Who the hell are you?!

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:54.910
I'm Subaru, an employee of Imperial.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:15:00.580
What?! Imperial's supposed to be
the top company in all Gatepia!

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:05.500
Being the best doesn't make it fair
to snatch it from under our noses!

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:09.660
That's right! We're the ones
who defeated the maju!

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:12.250
I'm not being unfair.

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:16.910
I had already taken the kirakuri
well before you lot arrived.

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:23.790
I sneaked past the maju after
it crashed from working overtime.

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:25.540
It was sleeping?

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:31.700
Yes. These folks from Cyedge
here deliberately chose to fight it.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:33.000
Say "ahh!"

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.950
--He even made it eat a red-eyed Susan.
--Eat up! It's chow time!

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.000
You little...!

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.870
Because a true man doesn't
back down from a fight.

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:49.790
Sneaking past it to avoid battle is more
efficient and achieves the same result.

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:52.540
You have no room to complain.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:56.790
This must be what it's like
to be at a loss for words.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:59.000
I believe I've made my point.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:02.540
In that case, I'll be on
my way with this kirakuri.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:04.450
Goodbye.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:05.450
Wha--?!

00:16:05.450 --> 00:16:07.500
Sh-She's gone...

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:11.700
Employees that work for
the best sure are something else.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:17.200
Yeah... It's actually scary how good she is.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.200
Tsk!

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.370
Imperial, huh?

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:29.120
In the end, we didn't get first...

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:33.750
But still, at least we'll get a decent
reward for defeating the maju.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:37.750
We're one step closer
to paying the inheritance tax!

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:40.250
That's great and all, but...

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:41.620
Hmm?

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:44.000
Can you believe that guy?

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:47.330
I wish we could've made him eat his own words.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:51.330
Considering victory was pretty much ours,

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:56.450
I'll be a good sport and call it a tie! Later!

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.450
See what I mean?

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:03.370
Now, now. I'm just happy
you didn't get taken from us.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:08.000
Sheesh! You're such a softy sometimes.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.120
All's well that ends well.

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:13.000
Yeah. Can't wait to get home and relax.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:16.500
If you want to head home,
I'll take care of the rest.

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:17.910
Minato!

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:19.080
Hmm?

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:21.500
Huh? Um, aren't you...?

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.120
It's Valmi.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:26.500
Oh, yeah. Valmi. Need me for something?

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:30.080
Yup, that's right. Be honest.

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:33.500
You're not a normal person at all, are you?

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:37.080
Huh? No? I'm just a regular guy.

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:40.160
No need to be so modest.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:44.790
Earlier, you displayed incredible
knowledge and quick thinking.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:49.200
And furthermore,
brilliant command to defeat the maju.

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:54.250
Your qualifications as an adventurer
clearly exceed Rivar's.

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:56.950
Huh? No. That's not...

00:17:56.950 --> 00:18:00.620
Hopefully, this contest
was good medicine for him.

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:06.250
He's the kind of person who talks
like he's way better than he actually is.

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:10.790
Let's hope this experience
helps him learn a lesson or two.

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:16.200
And if it doesn't, I'll have to
thoroughly drill it into him myself.

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.580
Huh? V-Valmi?

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:21.410
W-Was she always like this?

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:26.330
More importantly, didn't you recently
leave a job that you had...

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:29.830
...and become the president of Kibou Company?

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.080
Y-Yeah, and?

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:34.620
I've heard rumors going around.

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:38.950
That an elite employee recently
left a certain top company.

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:41.620
I-Is that right?

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:45.410
Are you saying it's a terribly big coincidence?

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:48.160
Th-That's really all it is.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:51.660
Because I'm just an ordinary, newbie president.

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:59.910
Well, let's just leave it at that
for the time being.

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:03.620
President! What are you doing?!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:06.160
We're gonna leave you behind!

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.450
Yeah, okay! I'm coming!

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:11.410
Sorry, but I've gotta get going.

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:14.660
Sure. I hope we meet again soon!

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:20.000
It's like she's smiling,
but only on the outside...

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:22.330
This person seems like trouble.

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:28.450
Whew!

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:30.660
The others went home, huh?

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:36.660
They're all exhausted from fighting
that tough maju and almost losing you.

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:40.080
Mmm, yeah. Good point.

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:43.450
I'm leaving once I sort out this paperwork too.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.450
Oh. In that case, I can help.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:53.200
President... What were you
talking about earlier?

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:55.500
Huh? Earlier when?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:59.160
Um, with that woman from Cyedge.

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:03.330
Oh, Valmi? It was no big deal.

00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:06.700
Just... a bit about my last job.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:14.500
President. No, Minato.

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:17.500
You're not gonna quit, right?

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:19.750
Huh? No way.

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:25.910
But lately, with all the headhunting...
And Akari almost getting taken away...

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:31.080
Akari couldn't have said it better.
This company is like family.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:36.250
Well, it makes me mad!
It's just like insulting my family!

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:41.200
There's lots I'm not used to
and lots I've yet to learn.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:46.330
But I kinda feel at home here.
I've never thought about quitting.

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:47.450
But...

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:51.290
Besides, I'm the president of Kibou Company now.

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:55.450
President...

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:57.620
I guess you're right.

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:00.620
I'm sorry for saying something weird.

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:03.700
It's a pleasure to be
working with you, President.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:05.330
Yup. Same here.

00:21:27.830 --> 00:21:32.250
<i>Looking way up into the night sky</i>

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:36.830
<i>A pretty jewel caught my eye</i>

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:41.160
<i>Clear skies tomorrow sure would be nice</i>

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:45.290
<i>Now, make a wish upon a star</i>

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:47.370
<i>Lazily</i>

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:50.200
<i>Today comes to a close</i>

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:54.580
<i>Dead tired and worn out</i>

00:21:54.580 --> 00:22:01.080
<i>Good work</i>
<i>Let's do our best again tomorrow</i>

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:03.660
<i>Goodnight</i>

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:05.870
<i>Every day is sparkling</i>

00:22:05.870 --> 00:22:10.410
<i>Just like a box of jewels (sparkling)</i>

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:12.620
<i>And so brilliant</i>

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:14.830
<i>Any work undone</i>

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:19.370
<i>We'll leave for dreamland (sleep tight)</i>

00:22:19.370 --> 00:22:22.870
<i>Let's embark on adventure</i>

00:22:22.870 --> 00:22:27.160
<i>So sleep soundly tonight</i>

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:32.410
<i>And meet up with me in our dreams</i>

00:22:32.410 --> 00:22:35.500
<i>Sleep tight</i>

00:22:39.830 --> 00:22:42.120
It's good to be back!

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:44.870
Whew! Today was so rough!

00:22:44.870 --> 00:22:48.450
You were huffing and puffing the entire time.

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:50.250
Talk about out of shape.

00:22:51.750 --> 00:22:55.000
It might be wise to build up
your stamina, President.

00:22:56.660 --> 00:22:58.450
Sorry.

00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:01.200
Great work, everyone!

00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:04.200
I prepared some sweets
and black tea for you all!

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:07.580
Thank you!

00:23:07.580 --> 00:23:08.750
Let's eat!

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:15.790
This castella's so good!

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:21.370
She's a hard worker and thoughtful
to boot! Guide's truly the best!

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:22.870
Why, thank you.

00:23:22.870 --> 00:23:25.620
Huh? Where's Yutoria?

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:29.160
Yutoria's been out of the office since morning.

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:32.410
Oh, Yutoria!

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:35.040
B-Big news!

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:37.870
Wh-What are you so worked up about?

00:23:37.870 --> 00:23:39.000
I...!

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:40.330
I?

00:23:40.330 --> 00:23:41.750
I...

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:44.120
I made a juicy discovery!

00:23:47.500 --> 00:23:49.750
A juicy discovery?
